decreasing by a factor of 2 every 16 months. Compared to 2012, it now takes 44 times less compute to train a neural network to the level of AlexNet (by contrast, Moore’s Law would yield an 11x cost improvement over this period). Our results suggest that for AI tasks with high levels of recent investment, algorithmic progress has yielded more gains than classical hardware efficiency.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"AI and efficiency","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/ai-and-efficiency"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"6a5bbc87f5a646548132c70267a4f14870b041657af90f4a25507ea6dc8a07c8","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/jukebox","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"3039e4df07aab690a6de","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/jukebox","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2020-04-30T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re introducing Jukebox, a neural net that generates music, including rudimentary singing, as raw audio in a variety of genres and artist styles. We’re releasing the model weights and code, along with a tool to explore the generated samples.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Jukebox","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/jukebox"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"b39097866943829e88fb9ede341731f1d9f83fb782b2b3f6e16ae13ed75bfd4e","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/improving-verifiability","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"a77a394cc7a9e9f5ee8b","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"http